  "body": "## Purpose and scope\n\nComplete Task-02's nine Linux x64 components so Core negotiation and binding contracts, database codecs, providers, transactions and bounded result streams can be composed against the pinned design. A01/B01 are reused from Task-01. Design remains pinned to `c62cdb8aee833b6ab1a03e29a3f59f81a1b483f9`.\n\nCompanion evidence PR: https://github.com/IzuSharp/Plan/pull/14\n\nAll nine Linux component scopes are implemented, validated and independently reviewed. Owned API/XML documentation, guides, examples and necessary tests accompany the implementation.\n\n| Task | Delivered scope | Principal Linux evidence |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| A02 | Status, capability and compatibility negotiation | 84 exact API/XML symbols; 26 isolated cases and 428 assertions in each JIT/AOT mode |\n| A05 | Error and panic conversion boundaries | JIT 69/AOT 70 assertions; 23 independent probes |\n| A09 | Binding-contract IR and input validation | JIT 220/AOT 221 assertions; 14 independent probes; all six review findings closed |\n| B05 | Transactions, connection recovery and Unknown | 79 symbols; 29 managed assertions per mode; actual-provider acceptance completed with B02/B03 |\n| B07 | Fallible Rust parameter codecs | 120 actual-provider codec vectors and 4,189 malformed rejections per fixture mode |\n| B09 | Minimal query bindings, metadata and relationships | 42 exact Cdecl declarations; 16 native groups; JIT 66/AOT 67 assertions |\n| B02 | PostgreSQL execution adapter | PostgreSQL 18.0; 11 actual provider groups; 22 managed assertions per JIT/AOT mode |\n| B03 | SQLite execution adapter | SQLite 3.51.3; 14 actual provider groups; 36 managed assertions per JIT/AOT mode |\n| B06 | Bounded result batches and streams | Both providers; 598 assertions and 58 recorded cases in each JIT/AOT mode |\n\n## Integration and review\n\n- B05/B06's provider acceptance dependencies are closed within this batch. PostgreSQL response-loss testing proves a durable COMMIT while the client reports Unknown; provider retirement and same-session recovery are exercised.\n- Streaming tests account for up to two retained provider rows including handoff, distinguish owned byte budgets from process measurements, and verify zero live reservations/owners/copies after cleanup.\n- Every task has an independent accepted review. B09 has separate native and managed reviews; retained regressions cover logical owner closure, provider parent-lease retirement, capability gates and cancellation ownership.\n- Six combined gates passed on clean `c62362de14799af88e85ca22977b9b4cce060d3d`: Rust formatting, warning-denied Clippy, Release workspace tests, existing native-asset build, locked restore and the **50-project Release solution build**, with zero managed warnings/errors.\n- [Final normal CI 43840288797](https://github.com/IzuSharp/NativeWeave/actions/runs/43840288797) passed on `25692f957adbf49430b26de8f6b2ece92418e058`.\n\nScoped CI follow-ups fix the B09 API checker's dictionary formatting and synchronize the SQLite cancellation test at controlled fetch/worker phases. The latter's 11 focused commands and actual JIT/AOT runs passed independent review; production inputs were unchanged. Original failures and the explicit receipt metadata erratum are retained. Gitleaks uses narrowly matched public-value exceptions with its default rules/full-history scan retained and positive canaries independently verified.\n\n## Evidence and recovery\n\nThe [Linux handoff](https://github.com/IzuSharp/Plan/blob/task/Task-02-linux/ledger/evidence/batches/Task-02/handoff-linux.md) links raw receipts, original failures and final reviews. All nine task branches have final remote source checkpoints in the [recovery map](https://github.com/IzuSharp/Plan/blob/task/Task-02-linux/ledger/evidence/batches/Task-02/remote-source-checkpoints-linux.json).\n\nGit Data publication preserves exact trees while assigning new commit identities. This PR's final remote head `25692f957adbf49430b26de8f6b2ece92418e058` and local integration `30c726aab64ab418d40364c8aa5ad9229d68dd78` share tree `155c26f13aa8cfb9ec3af68914e6cd879303f458`; original receipts retain their actual tested local commits.\n\n## Remaining closeout\n\nMerge both linked PRs through normal repository review/checks, then confirm the exact main merge CI and existing **HelloWorld-only** automatic preview: final `published-and-consumed`, signature verification, unsigned payload equality and actual registry JIT/AOT consumption.\n\nLinux component acceptance is complete. Other platforms remain unexecuted. Full B04 owning-host composition and pristine component-package consumption remain downstream gates; this PR adds no release package or ordinary-consumer Cargo step. Batch publication/merge closeout remains pending.\n",
